{title: Oh My Darling, Clementine}
{artist: Percy Montrose, 1884}
{key: C}
{license: public-domain}
{tempo: 96}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]In a cavern, in a [G7]canyon, exca[C]vating for a [G7]mine
[C]Dwelt a miner, forty-[F]niner, and his [G7]daughter Clemen[C]tine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Oh my darling, oh my [G7]darling, oh my [C]darling Clemen[G7]tine
[C]You are lost and gone for[F]ever, dreadful [G7]sorry, Clemen[C]tine
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Light she was and like a [G7]fairy, and her [C]shoes were number [G7]nine
[C]Herring boxes without [F]topses, sandals [G7]were for Clemen[C]tine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Drove she ducklings to the [G7]water every [C]morning just at [G7]nine
[C]Hit her foot against a [F]splinter, fell in[G7]to the foaming [C]brine
{end_of_verse}
